---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');

const aboutJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'AboutPage',
  name: 'About Nocturnus.AI',
  description:
    'Nocturnus.AI is building the context-infrastructure layer for the agent stack. Thesis, mission, and how we measure success.',
  url: 'https://nocturnus.ai/about',
  mainEntity: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'Nocturnus.AI',
    url: 'https://nocturnus.ai/',
    slogan: 'Reasoning for AI agents.',
  },
};
---

<Layout
  title="About — The context layer for agents | Nocturnus.AI"
  description="Why a context-infrastructure layer has to exist. What Nocturnus believes, how we measure ourselves, and how to get involved."
  keywords={['about nocturnus', 'mission', 'context server', 'ai agents', 'open source']}
  jsonLd={aboutJsonLd}
>
  <Navbar solid />

  <main class="about-shell">

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <!-- HERO — thesis statement                                            -->
    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="about-hero">
      <div class="site-container">
        <div class="site-kicker" style="color: var(--site-accent);">About</div>
        <h1 class="about-h1">
          The agent stack is missing a layer.<br/>
          <span class="about-accent">We're building it.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="about-lede">
          The model providers won't build this &mdash; they get paid by the token.
          The agent frameworks won't build this &mdash; they need to stay provider-neutral.
          The vector database vendors are solving an adjacent problem. It's going to be
          its own layer, and it's going to be infrastructure.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr class="section-rule" />

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <!-- THE THESIS                                                         -->
    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="site-section-tight">
      <div class="site-container" style="max-width: 860px;">
        <div class="site-kicker">The Thesis</div>
        <h2 class="about-h2">Most tokens an agent spends are paying the model to re&#8209;read what it just read.</h2>
        <p class="about-body">
          Every production agent today runs the same loop: take a goal, replay the entire conversation
          history, send it to the model, get back a response, repeat. At one user, it's invisible.
          At ten thousand users, the token bill is the line item that ate your gross margin.
          A $500 proof-of-concept becomes $847,000 per month without anyone changing a line of code.
        </p>
        <p class="about-body">
          The standard fixes don't fix it. Longer context windows make the prompt more expensive,
          not cheaper. Vector retrieval returns what <em>looks</em> similar, not what's <em>true</em>.
          Summarization compresses at the cost of fidelity. None of these are the same shape as the
          problem. The problem is that <strong>the agent sends the model information it already has,
          information it doesn't need, and information it can't rely on</strong>. The only correct
          answer is to send less, and to send the right less.
        </p>
        <p class="about-body">
          That's a computation. You can't retrieve your way into it, and you can't summarize your
          way into it. You have to <em>reason</em> about what's necessary, given the goal, given
          what's known. We are building a server that does exactly that &mdash; sitting between
          your agent and the LLM, deriving the minimum context required for the next decision,
          and returning only that.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr class="section-rule" />

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <!-- WHAT WE BELIEVE — the principles                                   -->
    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="site-section-tight">
      <div class="site-container">
        <div class="section-head reveal" style="max-width: 780px; margin-bottom: var(--space-5);">
          <div class="site-kicker">What We Believe</div>
          <h2 class="about-h2" style="margin-bottom: 0;">Five commitments that shape every design decision.</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="about-beliefs">
          <div class="plain-card about-belief">
            <div class="about-belief-idx">01</div>
            <h3>Similarity is not truth.</h3>
            <p>
              The nearest vector is not the correct answer. Agents that decide based on "the most
              semantically similar document" will hallucinate on operational state &mdash; current
              contract terms, current inventory, current customer tier. We return facts the way
              a logic engine returns facts: because they are provable from what's known.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="plain-card about-belief">
            <div class="about-belief-idx">02</div>
            <h3>Determinism is a product feature.</h3>
            <p>
              The same query should return the same answer. Twice. A hundred times. In production,
              non-determinism is a bug surface you can't close. The reasoning layer should be
              something you can reason about &mdash; not a probability distribution you have to
              audit after the fact.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="plain-card about-belief">
            <div class="about-belief-idx">03</div>
            <h3>Measurement beats marketing.</h3>
            <p>
              Every cost and compression claim we publish is derived from a live API call we can
              point to &mdash; and you can reproduce. Our benchmarks are in the repo. Our math is
              on the <a href={`${base}/calculations`}>calculations page</a>. If a number we publish
              doesn't match a measurement, it's a bug.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="plain-card about-belief">
            <div class="about-belief-idx">04</div>
            <h3>Be a layer, not a destination.</h3>
            <p>
              Agent teams shouldn't have to migrate off LangChain, LlamaIndex, CrewAI, Mastra,
              AutoGen, the OpenAI Agents SDK, or the Vercel AI SDK to use us. We plug in. We are
              invocable from everywhere, in every language, against every model. Infrastructure
              that everyone reaches for and nobody has to think about.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="plain-card about-belief">
            <div class="about-belief-idx">05</div>
            <h3>Open source is the only defensible path.</h3>
            <p>
              Infrastructure that sits between an agent and its model will only get trusted if
              it's auditable. The core engine is <a href="https://github.com/Auctalis/nocturnusai/blob/main/LICENSE" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BUSL-1.1</a> — free for internal use, converting to Apache 2.0 in 2030. The benchmarks, the math, and the
              decision logic are all in the open. If we get this wrong, you'll see it first.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr class="section-rule" />

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <!-- HOW WE MEASURE SUCCESS                                             -->
    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="site-section-tight">
      <div class="site-container" style="max-width: 860px;">
        <div class="site-kicker">How We Measure Success</div>
        <h2 class="about-h2">Three numbers we care about, in order.</h2>

        <ol class="about-metrics">
          <li>
            <div class="about-metric-name">Token reduction on real workloads.</div>
            <p>
              Not synthetic benchmarks. Not cherry-picked conversations. The hard number an agent
              team can report to their CFO. Today, that number is <strong>82&ndash;90% on live
              Claude Opus 4 and Gemini 2.0 Flash</strong> for a 15-turn product-support
              conversation. Next quarter, we want it higher, on harder workloads.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <div class="about-metric-name">Integration breadth, not depth.</div>
            <p>
              We would rather be the default option in ten frameworks than the best option in one.
              Native adapters for LangChain, LlamaIndex, CrewAI, AutoGen, MCP, Mastra, the OpenAI
              Agents SDK, and the Vercel AI SDK &mdash; all invocable in one line. The number we
              track is <em>time-to-first-context-call</em>.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <div class="about-metric-name">Correctness under retraction.</div>
            <p>
              When a fact becomes false, everything derived from it should become false with it.
              When a premise is removed, the context window should update without developer
              intervention. This is not a cost feature. It's a correctness feature &mdash; and
              it's why we built the truth-maintenance system before we shipped the cache.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr class="section-rule" />

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <!-- WHERE WE STAND                                                     -->
    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="site-section-tight">
      <div class="site-container" style="max-width: 860px;">
        <div class="site-kicker">Where We Stand</div>
        <h2 class="about-h2">This is a v0.3 product, shipping in public.</h2>
        <p class="about-body">
          The core engine, the HTTP API, the MCP server, the Python and TypeScript SDKs, the
          LangChain adapter, and the live benchmark are all in the repo and running today. The
          roadmap &mdash; deeper integrations, better measurement, first-party hosted tier &mdash;
          is on <a href="https://github.com/Auctalis/nocturnusai" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.
        </p>
        <p class="about-body">
          We are a small team. We answer issues. We take pull requests. We take strong opinions
          from people building agents in production, because those are the people whose pain we
          are trying to solve.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr class="section-rule" />

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <!-- GET INVOLVED                                                       -->
    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="site-section cta-band">
      <div class="site-container">
        <div class="section-head reveal">
          <h2 class="site-title" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem); color: var(--site-dark-text);">Get involved.</h2>
          <p style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.78rem; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.45); margin-top: 0.5rem;">
            SOURCE AVAILABLE &middot; BUSL-1.1 &rarr; APACHE 2.0 (2030) &middot; BUILDING IN PUBLIC
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: var(--space-5);" class="reveal">
          <a href="/nocturnus-one-pager.png" download="Nocturnus-AI-One-Pager.png" class="button-secondary" style="font-size: 0.95rem; padding: 0.75rem 1.8rem;">
            Download one-pager (PNG) &darr;
          </a>
          <p style="font-size: 0.78rem; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.4); margin-top: 0.6rem;">
            Architecture, math, integrations, and mission &mdash; one image, print-friendly.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="statement-grid reveal reveal-delay-1">
          <div class="plain-card" style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.04); border-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.12); box-shadow: none;">
            <h3 style="color: var(--site-dark-text);">Try the engine</h3>
            <p style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.72);">Docker one-liner, no signup. Running in 10 seconds.</p>
            <div class="button-row" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
              <a href={`${base}/docs`} class="button-primary">Start Here &rarr;</a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="plain-card" style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.04); border-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.12); box-shadow: none;">
            <h3 style="color: var(--site-dark-text);">Run the benchmark</h3>
            <p style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.72);">Reproduce every number we publish &mdash; or break them.</p>
            <div class="button-row" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
              <a href={`${base}/benchmark`} class="button-secondary">Benchmark &rarr;</a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="plain-card" style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.04); border-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.12); box-shadow: none;">
            <h3 style="color: var(--site-dark-text);">Contribute</h3>
            <p style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.72);">Issues, PRs, design-partner pilots. We read everything.</p>
            <div class="button-row" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
              <a href="https://github.com/Auctalis/nocturnusai" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="button-secondary">GitHub &rarr;</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p style="text-align: center; margin-top: var(--space-5); font-size: 0.95rem; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.6);">
          For partnerships, press, or design-partner pilots: <a href="mailto:hello@nocturnus.ai" style="color: var(--site-accent); font-weight: 500;">hello@nocturnus.ai</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .about-shell { background: var(--site-bg); }

  .about-hero {
    padding: 7.5rem 0 3rem;
  }
  .about-hero > .site-container { max-width: 860px; }

  .about-h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5vw, 3.8rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin: 0.6rem 0 1.4rem;
  }
  .about-accent { color: var(--site-accent); }

  .about-lede {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.72;
    color: var(--site-muted);
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .about-h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.2rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0.6rem 0 1.4rem;
  }

  .about-body {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.72;
    color: var(--site-text);
    margin: 0 0 1.2rem;
  }
  .about-body em { color: var(--site-muted); }
  .about-body a {
    color: var(--site-accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .about-beliefs {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
  .about-belief {
    padding: var(--space-4);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--site-accent);
    position: relative;
  }
  .about-belief-idx {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--site-accent);
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }
  .about-belief h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  .about-belief p {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--site-muted);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .about-belief a { color: var(--site-accent); }

  .about-metrics {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    counter-reset: metric;
  }
  .about-metrics li {
    counter-increment: metric;
    padding: 1.2rem 0 1.2rem 3rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--site-line);
    position: relative;
  }
  .about-metrics li:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .about-metrics li::before {
    content: counter(metric, decimal-leading-zero);
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 1.3rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--site-accent);
  }
  .about-metric-name {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .about-metrics p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--site-muted);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .about-metrics strong { color: var(--site-text); }
  .about-metrics em { color: var(--site-text); font-style: italic; }
</style>
